    {
      "id": "p0150-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "As we've already seen, Papyrus' Japanese text is written vertically from top to bottom, moving from right to left. This style of writing Japanese has been around for centuries. But what happens when foreign characters and symbols appear in vertical Japanese text?",
        "raw": "As we've already seen, Papyrus' Japanese text is written vertically from top\nto bottom, moving from right to left. This style of writing Japanese has been\naround for centuries. But what happens when foreign characters and symbols\nappear in vertical Japanese text?",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29213402,
          0.65432857,
          0.89304869,
          0.72226429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2896084,
          0.65361429,
          0.90466452,
          0.72333571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          23,
          24,
          25,
          26
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "前面已经看到，Papyrus 的日文采用竖排，从上往下读，再从右向左移列。日语沿用这种写法已有几百年。不过，竖排日文中出现外文字母和符号时，该怎么办？",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.29258393,
          0.6529,
          0.90261948,
          0.72583571
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
        "font_weight": 450,
        "background": "transparent",
        "text_align": "justify",
        "auto_height": true,
        "limit_bottom": 0.8142857142857143,
        "snap_to_guides": true,
        "resize_anchor": "left"
      },
      "calibration": {
        "bbox": [
          0.29258393,
          0.6529,
          0.90261948,
          0.72583571
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "leading": 29.0
      },
      "review_issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0150-b011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "There are different methods of handling vertical foreign text - one common practice is to rotate the foreign characters before displaying them vertically, even though the surrounding Japanese characters aren't rotated. This is why the English word \"COOL\" appears sideways during the date with Papyrus.",
        "raw": "There are different methods of handling vertical foreign text - one common\npractice is to rotate the foreign characters before displaying them vertically,\neven though the surrounding Japanese characters aren't rotated. This is why\nthe English word \"COOL\" appears sideways during the date with Papyrus.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29394388,
          0.73669286,
          0.88573767,
          0.80430714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2896084,
          0.73597857,
          0.90466452,
          0.80537857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          27,
          28,
          29,
          30
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "竖排中的外文有不同处理方法。常见的一种是先把外文字母旋转，再排进竖行，周围的日文则保持原方向。这也就是约会时英文“COOL”（酷）会侧着出现的原因。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
